# KiCad — hardware/KiCad
#
# The project files (.kicad_pro/.kicad_sch/.kicad_pcb) sit directly in this
# directory, alongside the my-KiCad-library and wch_kicad_library submodules.
# That makes ${KIPRJMOD} resolve to this directory, so fp-lib-table and
# sym-lib-table load the submodules themselves rather than copies — which is
# the point of the layout.
#
# The repository root .gitignore already covers the lock/autosave/backup
# families for the whole tree; the essentials are repeated here so this folder
# stays correct if it is ever copied out on its own, which is how KiCad
# projects usually travel. What the root does not cover, and this file adds,
# is fabrication output.
#
# Note that a `#` only starts a comment at the START of a line — a trailing
# one becomes part of the pattern. Hence the comment-above-pattern style
# throughout.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, because they are sources:
#   *.kicad_pro    net classes, design rules, board stackup, plot setup
#   *.kicad_sch    schematic
#   *.kicad_pcb    board
#   fp-lib-table   library tables
#   sym-lib-table

# ---- Session state: per-user, per-machine, never shared ----
# Panel layout, last-used layer, local plot directory. Committing it means
# every collaborator's KiCad window fights over the same file.
*.kicad_prl
# Regenerated on demand by scanning the footprint libraries.
fp-info-cache

# ---- Lock files: present only while KiCad has the project open ----
*.lck
~*.lck

# ---- Autosave and backups ----
_autosave-*
# KiCad's own timestamped zip archive of the whole project.
*-backups/
*.bak
*-bak
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.kicad_sch-bak
*.000
*~

# ---- Rescue libraries ----
# Regenerated by the symbol rescue dialog when a project is opened against a
# library that has moved on.
*-rescue.lib
*-rescue.dcm
*-rescue.kicad_sym

# ---- Fabrication and export output ----
# All of it regenerable from the sources above. If a fab package for a build
# that was actually ordered needs archiving, commit it under a dated folder
# and add a `!` exception for that one folder — do not un-ignore the pattern.
/gerbers/
/production/
/fab/
*.gbr
*.gbrjob
*.drl
*.ncd
# Component placement / pick-and-place.
*.pos
# DRC and ERC reports.
*.rpt
# Netlist — regenerated from the schematic.
*.net
# Specctra export to an external router, and the session file back from it.
*.dsn
*.ses

# ---- 3D and document exports of this board ----
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: these must not catch the .step and
# .zip vendor assets that live inside the library folders.
/wire-encoder-modbus-interface.step
/wire-encoder-modbus-interface.stp
/wire-encoder-modbus-interface.wrl
/wire-encoder-modbus-interface.pdf

# ---- Editor ----
# vscode-local-history
.history/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file does not reach into the submodules
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# my-KiCad-library/ and wch_kicad_library/ are separate repositories. Git does
# not apply a parent .gitignore inside a submodule, and this repo records only
# their commit hashes — so anything created loose inside them is invisible to
# `git status` here, and is not backed up by committing this project.
#
# That matters because the footprint libraries this board loads live in there.
# A footprint added straight into my-KiCad-library/ without being committed
# and pushed to that repository exists on one disk only.
